node_modules/
dist/
release/
*.log
.DS_Store
test-vault/.geode/*
!test-vault/.geode/plugins/
test-vault/.geode/plugins/*
!test-vault/.geode/plugins/status-probe/
!test-vault/.geode/plugins/menu-probe/
# Third-party Bases plugin (MIT) used by tests/e2e/bases-plugin-view.spec.ts
# and tests/e2e/bases-kanban-interaction.spec.ts as the real-world check that a
# Bases view registers, renders and writes. Its published *release assets* are
# checked in (digests pinned in the directory's README-geode.md) so the tests
# exercise the artifact users actually install rather than a local build or a
# hand-written stand-in. Disabled by default, like status-probe.
!test-vault/.geode/plugins/kanban-bases-view/
# The Ivory theme ships with the demo vault so it's installed and selectable
# out of the box in Settings -> Appearance -> Themes. Other themes dropped
# into test-vault/.geode/themes/ locally stay ignored.
!test-vault/.geode/themes/
test-vault/.geode/themes/*
!test-vault/.geode/themes/Ivory/
# Starter-vault prototype (resources/starter-vault/, see Compass doc
# bacd8621): only app.json is a deliberate, checked-in seed (theme: light +
# cssTheme: Ivory, the desired default for a new user's first open). Every
# other .geode/* entry is per-run indexer/workspace/community state that a
# live Geode session writes back into this folder the moment it's opened
# (metadata-cache/, workspace.json, community.json, device-reconcile:*) and
# must never be committed.
resources/starter-vault/.geode/*
!resources/starter-vault/.geode/app.json
test-results/
playwright-report/
.benchmark-vault/
.benchmark-results/
ios/App/CapApp-SPM/.build/
ios-mvp-artifacts/
**/xcuserdata/
ios/App/CapApp-SPM/.swiftpm/
